  "details": "Over the past 2 weeks I have noticed a reoccurring problem with a burst of many disconnections over a few hour period. For me this has mainly been happening late at night when I am afk/sleeping, so I only notice it when I wake up. I will be in a world for a while with no problems, and then suddenly I will error out and get sent to my home world (This is also something I might make another post on, instead of getting properly reconnected, I get sent to a new home instance, it's incredibly annoying). Then, anywhere from 1 to 10 minutes later I error out again, and get sent to a (new) home instance again. This will then repeat for an hour or two straight. Apparently this morning I had 21 total reconnects before everything stabilized. I have added a graph of the length and number of instances I was in this morning. I also understand that there is a chance this may be related to an internet problem on my side, in the past I have had problems with lightly shaky internet. It's not been bad enough to cause problems with most things I do, but vrchat has been an exception to that every now and again. If that is the case, I would still consider this a problem due to how the errors and subsequent reconnections were handled. I get thrown out of the original instance, and then have 21 new ones made. I will say though, this is a bit better than the old *disconnection noise* and getting stuck in a disconnection menu void until you realize what happened.",
